.TH DANBY-AEROBRAKING 1
.SH NAME
danby-aerobraking \- orbital energy loss during atmospheric passes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/aerobraking
.SH MODEL
Central gravity produces the orbit while exponential atmosphere applies drag
near planetary radius. Repeated periapsis passages lower speed and apoapsis.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/aerobraking.b
.PP
A real command module, not a plugin implementing the bespoke
.IR orbital (2)
interface: it just prints its own spec (title, parameters, initial
state, and both the central-gravity and atmospheric-drag terms as
literal
.IR eqn (7)
strings - see
.IR eqn2hoc (2))
when run, exactly like any other command in this tree. Driven by
.B /appl/temple/eqnorbital.b,
a harness that reads and evaluates that spec directly - no separate
module interface, and no separate parsing library either. See
.IR eqnorbitaltest (1).
